# AMD GPU MES Hang - System Freeze
# Date: 2026-01-14 17:31
# Kernel: 6.18.4-3-cachyos-wifi-fix
# Status: SYSTEM FREEZE - Required force reboot

## Summary
System froze approximately 2 minutes after resume from sleep. AMD discrete GPU's
MES (Micro Engine Scheduler) failed to respond, causing complete system hang.
This is NOT a WiFi issue - MT7925 had no errors at time of freeze.

## Root Cause
AMD GPU MES failure after suspend/resume:
  amdgpu 0000:c2:00.0: amdgpu: MES failed to respond to msg=MISC (WAIT_REG_MEM)

## Timeline
- 17:29:46 - System resumed from sleep
- 17:29:46 - GPU re-initialized (ring assignments logged)
- 17:29:48 - WiFi reconnected successfully
- 17:31:46 - GPU MES failure (WAIT_REG_MEM timeout)
- 17:32:07 - Chrome detected GPU state invalid
- 17:32:14 - Chrome GPU process crashed (exit_code=512)
- After 17:32:14 - System completely frozen, required force reboot

## Related Issues During Session
- Bluetooth hci0 errors (Opcode 0x2041 failed: -16) - ongoing, unrelated to freeze
- Touchpad jump warnings from libinput - cosmetic
- kwin output configuration failed - display manager issue

## Hardware
- GPU: AMD discrete (0000:c2:00.0) - likely RX 7000 series in Framework 16
- This is the discrete GPU, not the integrated Radeon 890M

